Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic catalog** audit of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10.0
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]`. Mystery Guest, Eager Test, and Sleepy Test severities are downgraded per calibration rules. The in-memory SQLite fixture is hermetic and does **not** trigger Mystery Guest.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4** (of 8)   |

---

## Findings by Severity

### ① Conditional Test Logic — **High**

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, method `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** An `if`/`else` branch determines which assertion runs. If `loaded` is never a `PremiumUser`, the discount-rate path is dead code that silently passes. If it is, the name check never runs. Either way, half the test is untested.

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch may never execute, giving false coverage and hiding a regression.

---

### ② Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — **High**

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, method `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion
}
```

**Problem:** The test exercises `Insert` 100 times but never asserts anything. MSTest reports it as "passed" as long as no exception is thrown. The name implies a DoesNotThrow intent, but it would also pass if every insert silently failed and returned without persisting data.

**Fix — add a meaningful assertion:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 100 % pass rate even if the bulk path silently drops records.

---

### ③ Sleepy Test — **Medium** *(downgraded from High; integration calibration applied)*

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, method `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← blocks thread for 3 seconds

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
}
```

**Problem:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` hard-codes a 3-second wall-clock wait. This is non-deterministic (may be too short on slow CI, always too long on fast machines), blocks the thread (in an `async` method, no less), and inflates suite runtime.

**Fix — poll with a timeout or use an async wait mechanism:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
    var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();
    while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
    {
        Assert.IsTrue(sw.Elapsed < timeout, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; unnecessary 3-second penalty per run; thread blocked inside an `async` method.

---

### ④ Assertion Roulette — **Medium**

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, method `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Problem:** Four assertions, none with a failure message. When one fails in CI, the stack trace shows a line number but no human-readable context. At 3+ message-less assertions, diagnosis cost rises sharply (Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020).

**Fix — add descriptive messages:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip through the database");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip through the database");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Persisted user should have a positive database-assigned Id");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage when a nightly build fails on one of four unlabelled assertions.

---

## Smells Scanned and **Not Found** (15 of 19 — Clean)

| Smell | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | SQLite in-memory is hermetic; no files/network/env vars |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` and `10` in count assertions are contextually self-documenting |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` in any test |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by all 8 tests |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` or `Skip` attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No duplicated assertion statements |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Tests that share `Insert` use it for setup, not as the action under test |
| Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean | Correctly uses `[TestInitialize]` |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Class name is descriptive |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` or logging in tests |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | In-memory DB created in setup; no assumed-external resources |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | No empty method bodies |

Well-designed tests worth calling out: `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, and `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` are clean, focused, and properly assert outcomes.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** (`BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`) | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` after the loop | 2 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** (`GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`) | Split into two type-specific tests | 10 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** (`NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`) | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-with-timeout | 10 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** (`InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`) | Add message strings to all four assertions | 3 min |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests are clean. The other 4 each have exactly one smell. Fixes 1 and 4 are one-liners; fixes 2 and 3 need modest refactoring. No systemic design issues — this is a solid integration suite that needs targeted cleanup.
